4"],"note":"Chapter 574 is cruelty to animals, the main state animal law. Leash and licensing rules are county ordinance."},{"id":"skateboard","colloquial":["skateboard","skating","rollerblades","scooter park"],"statutory":["play vehicle","coasting"],"chapters":["484B"]},{"id":"trespass","colloquial":["trespassing","private property","no trespassing","cutting through"],"statutory":["trespass","unlawful entry"],"chapters":["207"],"note":"NRS 207.200, 'Unlawful trespass upon land; warning against trespassing'."},{"id":"noise","colloquial":["loud music","noise complaint","party too loud","party","loud"],"statutory":["noise","breach of the peace"],"chapters":["244","268","269"],"note":"State law does not set a noise limit. It authorises counties (NRS 244.363), cities (NRS 268.412) and towns to do it, so the real answer is always local. Pointing here at least tells the user that."},{"id":"truancy","colloquial":["skipping school","skip school","ditching","ditch school","cutting class","missing school","not going to school","absent"],"statutory":["truant","truancy","attendance"],"chapters":["392","385A"],"note":"Chapter 392 is PUPILS; NRS 392.040-392.220 cover attendance and habitual truancy."},{"id":"bullying","colloquial":["bullied","bullying","getting bullied","picked on","cyberbullying","cyber bullying","harassed at school"],"statutory":["bullying","cyber-bullying"],"chapters":["388"],"note":"NRS 388.122 defines bullying; 388.135 covers discrimination and cyber-bullying."},{"id":"school-discipline","colloquial":["expelled","expulsion","suspended","suspension","kicked out of school","in trouble at school","detention at school"],"statutory":["expulsion","suspension of pupil"],"chapters":["392"],"note":"Chapter 392 carries pupil discipline."},{"id":"theft","colloquial":["stole","stolen","someone stole","theft","stealing","took my stuff","robbed","my bike got stolen"],"statutory":["larceny","grand larceny","petit larceny","robbery","burglary"],"chapters":["205"],"note":"Chapter 205 is CRIMES AGAINST PROPERTY. Larceny is the statutory word, never 'stealing'."},{"id":"shoplifting","colloquial":["shoplifting","shoplift","stealing from a store","caught stealing"],"statutory":["shoplifting","larceny"],"chapters":["597","205"],"note":"NRS 597.850 is the merchant-detention statute; 205 carries the crime."},{"id":"vandalism","colloquial":["vandalism","graffiti","tagging","spray paint","keyed a car","broke a window","damaged property"],"statutory":["graffiti","malicious mischief"],"chapters":["206","244"],"note":"Chapter 206 is MALICIOUS MISCHIEF. Counties also regulate graffiti (244)."},{"id":"assault-battery","colloquial":["jumped me","beat me up","hit me","punched","fight","got in a fight","assaulted","attacked"],"statutory":["battery","assault"],"chapters":["200"],"note":"Chapter 200 is CRIMES AGAINST THE PERSON."},{"id":"harassment","colloquial":["harassment","stalking","stalker","wont leave me alone","threatening me","restraining order"],"statutory":["harassment","stalking","protection order"],"chapters":["200","033"],"note":"Chapter 033 carries protection orders; 200 the underlying crimes."},{"id":"wages","colloquial":["boss wont pay","not getting paid","my paycheck","minimum wage","overtime","unpaid wages","tips"],"statutory":["wages","minimum wage","overtime"],"chapters":["608"],"note":"Chapter 608 is COMPENSATION, WAGES AND HOURS."},{"id":"renting","colloquial":["renting","rent","apartment","lease","my landlord","tenant","roommate"],"statutory":["rental agreement","landlord","dwelling"],"chapters":["118A"],"note":"Chapter 118A is LANDLORD AND TENANT: DWELLINGS."},{"id":"deposit","colloquial":["security deposit","deposit back","wont return my deposit"],"statutory":["security deposit"],"chapters":["118A"],"note":"NRS 118A.242 caps the deposit at 3 months rent."},{"id":"eviction","colloquial":["evicted","eviction","kicked out of my apartment","notice to quit"],"statutory":["eviction","summary eviction"],"chapters":["040","118A"],"note"