 and 202.3653 onward carry concealed firearm rules."},{"id":"hunting-license","colloquial":["hunting license","fishing license","tags","draw a tag"],"statutory":["hunting license","fishing license","tag"],"chapters":["502"],"note":"Chapter 502 is LICENSES, TAGS AND PERMITS."},{"id":"school-search","colloquial":["school search my phone","principal searched","locker search","phone taken at school"],"statutory":["pupil","search"],"chapters":["392"],"note":"Chapter 392 is PUPILS. Nevada has little on-point statute here; results may be thin."},{"id":"id-required","colloquial":["do i have to show id","give my name","id to a cop"],"statutory":["identification"],"chapters":["171"],"note":"NRS 171.123 covers detention and identification."},{"id":"noise-party","colloquial":["loud party","noise complaint","music too loud","neighbors complained"],"statutory":["noise"],"chapters":["244","268"],"note":"Duplicate of the noise concept but with party phrasing."},{"id":"weapons","colloquial":["knife","pocket knife","pocketknife","blade","switchblade","brass knuckles","carry a knife","weapon","weapons","taser","pepper spray"],"statutory":["dangerous weapon","deadly weapon"],"chapters":["202","392"],"note":"'knife' appears in exactly one NRS heading, in HEALING ARTS. The statutory term is 'dangerous weapon' (chapter 202), and chapter 392 covers weapons at school."}]